  "why": "TypeScript callers into CommonJS modules that export a renamed class, `{ Handler: Impl }`. The TypeScript front-end defers these calls to its own `finalize`, which never routed them through the JavaScript export map, and which finalizer ran first depended on the first file walked. `decoy.js` also declares a `class Handler` nothing exports; `plain.js` does not. The two modules sit at the root and the callers under `app/`, so a JavaScript file is walked first. Pass 4 lost every call into `plain` (no `Handler` node to land on), and sent both callers of `decoy` to the decoy. `app/k.ts` default-imports `base.js`, whose `module.exports = Base` is a default slot and not a member: TypeScript resolves the import under the local name, and the default is matched by that name.",
